From eea9bd1f4527f5e558998a9078dffb91c9e8f249 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lei Gong <gonglei25@huawei.com>
Date: Thu, 21 Aug 2025 14:42:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 953/960] downstream: iommu/ummu-core: introduce UMMU-CORE,
 basic configs

We introduce ummu-core, which acts as an extension of the current IOMMU
Framework. This patch initializes basic ummu-core configs. To keep the
flexibility of utilizing, the ummu-core can be compiled to a module or
built-in kernel image.

UMMU-CORE provides fundamental interfaces for ummu drivers to manage
ummu resources. It also provides public interfaces and defines programming
model to ub drivers.

The ummu driver must select ummu-core kconfigs.

Signed-off-by: Yuhao Zhang <yuhao.zhang@huawei.com>
Signed-off-by: Lei Gong <gonglei25@huawei.com>
Signed-off-by: Liu Shixin <liushixin2@huawei.com>
---
 config.aarch64                             |  5 +++++
 config.aarch64-64k                         |  5 +++++
 drivers/iommu/Kconfig                      |  1 +
 drivers/iommu/Makefile                     |  2 +-
 drivers/iommu/hisilicon/Kconfig            |  6 ++++++
 drivers/iommu/hisilicon/Makefile           |  3 +++
 drivers/iommu/hisilicon/ummu-core/Kconfig  | 11 +++++++++++
